    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n#   Datasets:⟨3⟩\n* * *\n ![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/630cf55b15433862cfc9556f/vGMHov0fX4FLRS8p88INC.png) ⟨28⟩\nAbstractPhil⟨28⟩\n/\nqwen-synth-characters-100-json-test⟨29⟩\nlike 0\nModalities:  Image ⟨30⟩ Text ⟨31⟩\nFormats:  parquet ⟨32⟩\nSize:  1K - 10K ⟨33⟩\nTags:  Synthetic ⟨34⟩ ai-generated ⟨35⟩ structured-captions ⟨36⟩ json-schema ⟨37⟩ benchmark ⟨38⟩\nLibraries:  Datasets ⟨39⟩ pandas ⟨40⟩ Polars ⟨41⟩ + 1\nLicense:\napache-2.0\n Dataset card ⟨29⟩ Data Studio ⟨42⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨43⟩ Community 1 ⟨44⟩\nDataset Viewer\n Auto-converted to Parquet⟨45⟩ API Embed  Duplicate⟨46⟩ Data Studio\nSubset (1)\ndefault · 1k rows\ndefault (1k rows)\nSplit (1)\ntrain · 1k rows\ntrain (1k rows)\nSQL\nConsole\nThe dataset viewer is not available for this split.\nParquet error: Scan size limit exceeded: attempted to read 1002541483 bytes, limit is 300000000 bytes Make sure that 1. the Parquet files contain a page index to enable random access without loading entire row groups2. otherwise use smaller row-group sizes when serializing the Parquet files \n\n```\nError code:   TooBigContentError\n\n```\n\nNeed help to make the dataset viewer work? Make sure to review how to configure the dataset viewer⟨47⟩, and open a discussion⟨48⟩ for direct support.\n  * Added columns (on top of the source schema)⟨49⟩\n  * Caption structuring quality (Qwen3.5-9B, json_mode, greedy)⟨50⟩\n  * Provenance⟨51⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨52⟩ qwen-synth-characters-100-json-test \nA **100-row bench-test slice** of `AbstractPhil/qwen-synth-characters`⟨53⟩ processed end-to-end by the qwen-test-runner **12-process extraction system** : the 11 deterministic specialist vision tasks (`tasks_json`) plus caption→JSON-schema structuring of all three prepared captions (`struct_*`). Built to measure wall-clock, schema conformance, and grounding before scaling to the full 60,847-row set.\n> These are **not real people** — every image is diffusion-generated. Rows were additionally **age-gated** with `nateraw/vit-age-classifier` (strict mode: reject expected_age<24 or minor-probability-mass>0.20); each row's `age_audit` records the gate's evidence.\n##   ⟨49⟩ Added columns (on top of the source schema)   \n| column  | content  |  \n| --- | --- |  \n| `age_audit`  | JSON — age-gate decision + evidence for this row  |  \n| `tasks_json`  | JSON — {task: output} for the 11 deterministic vision tasks  |  \n| `tasks_valid`  | JSON — {task: bool} schema validity per task  |  \n|  `struct_joycaption` / `struct_qwen35_4b` / `struct_animetimm`  | JSON — the caption structured into the slot-registry schema + scores (schema_valid, grounding_rate, coverage_rate, hallucinations)  |  \n| `fused_json`  | JSON — the **FusedScene** : entities (position/depth/saliency + stratified OWNED attributes via mask-containment), relations with continuous offsets, counts, shared basin (uncertain attributions, never guessed), scene + quality blocks  |  \n| `prompt_fused`  | the deterministic fused prompt rendered from `fused_json` (counts → entities → relations → basin → scene)  |  \n|  `fusion_confidence` / `fusion_s`  | overall fusion confidence scalar / per-row fusion wall-clock  |  \n|  `proc_width`, `proc_height`  | processing resolution the vision tasks ran at (coords in `tasks_json` are relative to THIS size, in each task's declared coord_space)  |  \n| `specialist_s`  | wall-clock seconds for this row's 11-task extraction  |  \n##   ⟨50⟩ Caption structuring quality (Qwen3.5-9B, json_mode, greedy)   \n| caption  | schema valid  | mean grounding  | mean coverage  | speed  |  \n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |  \n| `caption_joycaption`  | 999/1000 valid  | 0.980  | 0.549  | 0.3s/caption  |  \n| `caption_qwen35_4b`  | 1000/1000 valid  | 0.980  | 0.796  | 0.16s/caption  |  \n| `caption_animetimm`  | 997/1000 valid  | 0.995  | 0.752  | 0.24s/caption  |  \n##   ⟨51⟩ Provenance \n  * Source rows scanned: 1359 (age-gate rejects: 359, missing captions: 0)\n  * Specialist extraction: 0.47s/image mean on the bench GPU\n  * All specialist models are Apache-2.0/MIT (GroundingDINO-base, SAM-vit-base, Depth-Anything-V2-Small, SigLIP2-so400m, EasyOCR) — outputs are redistributable.\n  * Full methodology: the `qwen-test-runner` repo, `docs/VISION_PIPELINE.md`.\n\n\nSee `bench_manifest.json` in this repo for the machine-readable bench report.\nCopy to bucket new\nUse this dataset \n\nDownloads last month\n    70\nNumber of rows: 1,000 Total file size: 1 GB\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨54⟩ Privacy⟨55⟩ About⟨56⟩ Careers⟨57⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
